[-Battle camera recursive tracking half-step]
// Status: locally runtime verified for the reached camera state; incomplete;
// disabled pending the derived-gain phase fix and input-origin replay.
// Replaces each of the six vector-tracking calls in loaded BTL FUN_006D8EB0
// with a wrapper that converts its recursive gain k to 1-sqrt(1-k). Two 60 Hz
// substeps then compose to the clean 30 Hz gain in real arithmetic. At frame
// 2493 this made controller +0x88 bit-exact because its +0x17C gain stayed at
// 0.65. Controller +0x34/+0x38 remained wrong because their +0x178 gain and
// its +0x170/+0x174 inputs had themselves advanced on the added phase.
// This section therefore fixes the vector integrator only; it must be combined
// with Battle camera derived tracking-gain phase and the angular-rate section.
// Code uses the Current-only development reservation at 0x008F0200 and the
// call-site edits target loaded BTL addresses, so this is not yet portable.
